29:33Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-05T03:54:59Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T07:32:17Z","closed_at":"2026-11-05T07:32:17Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":1,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Project, step, and reason\n\nNightly issue pipeline, Next item 6b (decisions 77, 86 and 105). The nightly planner proposes a chain of dependent issues together, and today `issue.py ready` reports every open blocker as unmet, so a blocked issue can never be proposed beside its blocker.\n\n### What changes\n\n`issue.py ready OWNER/REPO#N --check --proposed-with OWNER/REPO#M`, repeatable and refused without `--check`. A named blocker passes when it is open, one of this issue's blockers, in the same repository, and its card on this issue's board is in Proposed. Every other Ready condition and every other open blocker are checked as before, and `--stacked-on` is unchanged.\n\n### Done when\n\nThe ready tests pass, including the new `--proposed-with` cases, CI is green on main after the merge, and ARCHITECTURE.md's row for `tools/workflow/issue.py` names the option.\n","closed_by":{"login":"sh4i-yurei","id":232996764,"node_id":"U_kgDODeM_nA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/232996764?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sh4i-yurei","html_url":"https://github.com/sh4i-yurei","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sh4i-yurei/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sh4i-yurei/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sh4i-yurei/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sh4i-yurei/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sh4i-yurei/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sh4i-yurei/orgs","repos_url":"https://